project

Jun Hong
CSCI4229/5229 Summer 2025


Interstellar - Dr. Miller's Planet. A tidal wave is about to engulf the ranger.

Credit: https://www.turbosquid.com/3d-models/interstellar-movie-model-1693389
Credit goes to Warner Brothers for the source material.

Used modified ex35 to obtain coordinates for Bezier curves. Tried to use it to build an astronaut but ran out of time. You can view it by pressing "M".

Used a Gaussian to model a tidal wave.

Used the Fourier solution to 2-dim wave equation to model the water.

Used GIMP to create the cube map.

Key bindings
 *  l          Toggle lighting on/off
 *  z/Z        Toggle light movement
 *  </>        Move light
 *  r/R        decrease/increase radius of light source
 *  t/T        decrease/increase ambient light
 *  y/Y        decrease/increase diffuse light
 *  u/U        decrease/increase specular light
 *  e/E        decrease/increase emitted light
 *  M          reveals incomplete astronaut
 *  c/C        decrease/increase height of wave
 *  m          Toggle between orthogonal, perspective, and first person
 *  +/-        Changes field of view for perspective
 *  w/s/a/d    Move forward, backward, strafe left, and strafe right in first-person mode
 *  n/N        Decrease/increase shininess
 *  []         Lower/rise light
 *  x          Toggle axes
 *  arrows     Change view angle
 *  PgDn/PgUp  Zoom in and out
 *  0          Reset view angle
 *  ESC        Exit